, "kind": "request", "version": 1, "change": "opened", "cause": "opened", "source": "forgejo"}, "summary": "now owes request:paper-repo#18 “Real-graph (d) explanation: two-factor hypothesis not supported by the Holme–Kim check” (v1, opened)"}, {"id": "8a76de3a-043d-5bf1-b3ac-994c8dc762aa", "at": 1795658024.6207914, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132328, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "130d3103895f2441047635535fb4a0a8", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "a10adda0-33ac-5425-a429-0ef48e04c7e7", "at": 1795658024.6245522, "until": 1795658024.8167064, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132329, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "130d3103895f2441047635535fb4a0a8", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (90 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "The Holme–Kim check does not support the two-factor reading, so I dropped it in Brief revision 17 and asked the report to change its text.\n\nOn mechanism (d) at d = 20, Holme–Kim behaves like BA, not like the real graphs. The regression bias is 0.67 for Holme–Kim against 0.68 for BA, and 0.20–0.25 for Stanford3 and ego-Facebook. The log RMSE ratio to DM is +0.33 against +0.34 for BA, and −0.62 to −0.89 for the real graphs. So neither clustering, nor a degree tail, nor both together reproduces the real-graph behaviour. A wide exposure spread goes with it (rank correlation −0.95 over nine graph families, one run each), but that is a description, not a test. The cause stays undiagnosed.\n\nThe (b) dispersion form s(HM/AM − 1) also held on the new graph families without refitting. For Holme–Kim the predicted biases were −0.141, −0.163 and −0.129 against realised −0.147, −0.164 and −0.127 at d = 20, 5 and 80. \"Falls with d\" does not hold for Holme–Kim or log-normal graphs, which matches the near-Poisson condition already in the Brief.\n\nI opened `paper-repo`#18, because the text still keeps tail-and-clustering as the hypothesis. I suggested replacement wording and left placement to the report.\n\nP6 block results (κ\\*, the controls, the tails) are still owed on `experiment-repo`#7."}}, {"id": "07dffb71-ea2e-5847-999c-55f4a0cd9751", "at": 1795658025.715147, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132421, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "130d3103895f2441047635535fb4a0a8", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "60621f46-e9aa-5d89-b238-b737ddb1054f", "at": 1795658025.7229314, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132422, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "130d3103895f2441047635535fb4a0a8", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "end_turn", "label": "message → end_turn", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "1fcba708-57b9-51d4-8f38-16a2b7106199", "at": 1795658025.743931, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132423, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session_info_update", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "130d3103895f2441047635535fb4a0a8", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session_info_update"}, {"id": "ae39cdaf-f1c3-5afd-b985-54283741c651", "at": 1795658026.8447628, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 132424, "layer": "worker", "category": "lifecycle", "kind": "session.end